    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96596" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέρνιον</span></b> , τό, some
		kind of meat difficult to digest, perh. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>breast</i> of an animal, or = Lat.
				<i>sterilicula</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i> Trall.<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν κρεῶν βούλβιον</span>
			(= Lat. <i>vulva</i>) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ ς. καὶ πόδες . . τῶν βοῶν ἢ
					ῥύγχη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					11.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέρνιον</span> and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέρνιν</span></b> , = Lat.
				<i>sterile</i> (in a list of eatables, betw.
			<i>ypogastrion</i> and <i>vulva</i>),
		<u>Gloss.</u>
